            <ArticleTitle>[Comparison between 64-slice computed tomography and coronary angiography in the diagnosis of coronary atherosclerosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>624-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To compare the accuracy of 64-slice computed tomography and coronary angiography in the diagnosis of coronary atherosclerosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The imaging data of both 64-slice computed tomography and coronary angiography in 65 patients were analyzed retrospectively.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Among the 455 coronary arteries evaluated, the sensitivity, specificity and accuracy of 64-slice computed tomography were 54.6%, 95.1%, and 85.5%, respectively.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">64-slice computed tomography has a good potential in the diagnosis of coronary atherosclerosis with excellent sensitivity and specificity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
